A||||7||Formula88||V8 Archie opinions?||||4||
Z||000000||Formula88||01-24-2001||01:38 PM||||So what does everyone think of V8 Archie and his work?  I'm considering a V8 swap and am looking for some references.  If this has been covered to death, please accept my apologies.  <P>------------------<BR>When you choke a smurf, what color does it turn?||||reg||4
Z||000001||Chris McDonald||01-24-2001||02:24 PM||||Everybody has an opinion of something.  It is up to you to sort between the opinion and the facts to make a personal decision.  <P>I built a V8 Fiero using the V8 Archie Master ($3,000) kit.  Since this was my first V8 swap I wanted to stay ahead of the learning curve by buying as much as possible from him.  Now, I could easily start out with his econo kit and supply the other parts and maybe save a few dollars.<P>His stuff does work.  However, you either need to pay him to do it, have a really good mechanic, or have strong personal mechanical skills, abilities, and tools.  It does not just drop in the car.  You will also need access to a good welding shop to finish things up as you measure and test fit. You also need plenty of space to work and a good secure system for lifting the car and installing the engine assembly.  His video gives a basic idea of safety concerns and suggestions for making the conversion go as easy as possible. <P>The only major problem I had with him was getting the parts on time.  It was my understanding the whole kit would arrive in about two weeks from the order date.  However, it took several months to get the parts in.  As you can guess, I was in panic mode after dumping $3,000 on my card and going for a long period of time without all the parts.  <P>However, I have talked to other people that received everything in the two week time frame as expected. <P>He will take all the time you need on the phone to answer questions and he will give plenty of helpful suggestions.  <P>Good luck.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||01-24-2001||02:43 PM||||Boy howdy, it's worm-can opening time! You will get a variety of opinions painting Archies as everything from a god to the anti-Christ himself. Here are some undisputable facts.<BR>  <BR>1.Archie is a high-proile guy. He makes the rounds to shows and meets so many folks know who he is.  It's difficult to be that visible without pissing someone off. However, he is also someone that the vast majority of his customers speak very highly of.<P>2. Archie has been in the game forever. Many contenders have come and gone while Archie has been doing his thing. A shoddy product and poor customer support wears out it's welcome quickly. Archie's kit remains the standard in the industry.<P>3.Archie is a grumpy old fart.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> He does have his detractors and I don't think he loses much sleep over what people think about him.  He can be quite outspoken, however, when prostylizing his viewpoint. And I think that is just fine with me.<P>I do think there are other swaps that can turn the Fiero into a road-burner, and each one has it's pros and cons. However, if you do chose small block Chevy as your weapon of choice, I'd say Archie is THE MAN.<P> <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000003||Black88GT||01-24-2001||08:59 PM||||The only post-Archie (after he did a swap on a Fiero) tale I have heard from someone who I trust is at this site.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.nytmare.org/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nytmare.org/fiero</A> <P>About his character, well everyone has an opinion on that and if we all share then it will just turn into one big flame war.  So check out that site for an non-discrimating account.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||01-24-2001||11:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B><BR>3.Archie is a grumpy old fart.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> He does have his detractors and I don't think he loses much sleep over what people think about him.  He can be quite outspoken, however, when prostylizing his viewpoint. And I think that is just fine with me.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This is exactly what I like about Archie! heheh<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||01-24-2001||11:34 PM||||I prefer a SC 3800 over a SBC Chevy, but if I did want a V8, I wouldn't hesitate to go to Archie.. and someday I might, for a choptop..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000006||Formula88||01-25-2001||12:27 AM||||Thanks for the info. I know opinions are like a**holes - everyone's got one.  So I just wanted to hear what was said.  I figure between the fanatical supporters and the ones crying heresey, the truth is somewhere in between.  I personally like the idea of a V8 Fiero, simply because I love the sound and feel of a V8.  If I can do a V8 conversion that looks and acts like the factory could have done it, so much the better.  And, if I'm going to do a conversion, why not go all out.  But I'd be willing to look at some info on 3800, 3.4 or even Supercharged 3800 swaps.  Don't want to rule out any options without exploring them fully...||||reg||6
